    (1681::bigint, jsonb_build_object(
      'queue_wait', 'This is a craft-beer café, not a door-controlled club. Walk-ins usually make sense, but brunch and cultural sessions can slow the kitchen; one recent guest waited more than an hour while later tables were served first. Reserve if a book event matters, and allow extra time when the room is visibly busy.',
      'best_nights', 'Come in daylight or early evening for beer, books and conversation. The women-founded project suits a thoughtful date, feminist reading stop or soft start before nightlife—not late dancing. Check the Teusaquillo calendar itself; events advertised by its Candelaria sister may not happen here.',
      'crowd_mix', 'Women, readers, craft-beer drinkers, neighbourhood creatives, couples and queer-friendly groups shape the room. Its feminist story challenges beer culture as male territory. The welcome is meaningful, but the venue is not documented as LGBTQ+-majority; expect locals and mainstream visitors together.',
      'dress_code', 'Anything clean and relaxed works: daytime layers, denim, a date-night shirt or colourful queer casual. There is no reported selection at the door. Bogotá evenings cool quickly, and the venue offers outdoor seating, so carry a light jacket. The atmosphere rewards curiosity about beer and books more than a polished look.',
      'staff_inclusivity', 'The project’s women-led, feminist identity is a strong cultural welcome, and the Teusaquillo branch is listed with wheelchair access. Service evidence is thinner and one 2026 brunch account describes severe delays and unfair order handling. Ask about step-free routing and flag timing needs before placing a meal order.',
      'venue_classification', 'active_teusaquillo_women_founded_feminist_craft_beer_cafe_and_bookish_cultural_space_with_broad_queer_friendly_welcome_but_no_verified_lgbtq_majority',
      'source_urls', to_jsonb(array['https://www.facebook.com/diosacerveceria/','https://es.restaurantguru.com/Diosa-Cerveceria-Bogota','https://www.elespectador.com/el-magazin-cultural/daniela-villamizar-la-mujer-que-quiso-devolverle-la-feminidad-a-la-cerveza/','https://www.lafm.com.co/sociedad/matorral-libros-y-cerveza-en-un-rincon-unico-de-bogota-358080','https://www.bienalbogota.com/sites/default/files/2025-09/Bog25_Directorio_Distritos_Creativos_Agenda_Alterna_v20250925.pdf','https://visitbogota.co/sites/default/files/2026-06/Gu%C3%ADa%20LGBTI%20Digital%20ok.pdf']::text[]),
